{%- doc -%}
  Renders the BMP variant-price treatment: a "From <min>" prefix for a product
  whose variants differ in price.

  Emits nothing at all (not even whitespace) when the feature is off, when the
  product has a single price, or when the surface gate decides the shopper has
  already chosen a variant. snippets/price.liquid captures this output and
  falls back to the stock price string whenever it is blank, which is what
  keeps the off state byte-identical to stock Horizon.

  Takes no `price` param on purpose: this runs after price.liquid:73, where the
  stock `price` local has already been money-formatted. The money filter is
  applied here, last, to the product's own price_min — never to the stock
  `price_min` local, which price.liquid leaves null on any product page
  without volume pricing.

  @param {product} product_resource - The product being priced
  @param {boolean} use_currency - Format with money_with_currency instead of money
  @param {boolean} is_product_card - True on card surfaces, false on product pages
  @param {boolean} [bmp_show_from] - Per-block override resolved by blocks/price.liquid; nil falls back to settings.bmp_price_from_show (allow_false keeps an explicit false from being swallowed)

  @example
  {%- capture bmp_variation_price -%}
    {%- render 'bmp-price-variation', product_resource: product_resource, use_currency: use_currency, is_product_card: is_product_card, bmp_show_from: bmp_show_from -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign bmp_show = bmp_show_from | default: settings.bmp_price_from_show, allow_false: true

  unless product_resource.price_varies
    assign bmp_show = false
  endunless

  # Surface gate (spec 4.2). Cards ignore selection on purpose: Shopify sets
  # product.selected_variant by relevance on filtered collections and search
  # (documented at snippets/variant-swatches.liquid:78), which is not a
  # shopper's choice. Suppressing the label there would hide it on exactly the
  # surfaces carrying the most legal exposure. Product pages do clear the
  # label, once the shopper has actually picked.
  unless is_product_card
    if product_resource.selected_variant != blank
      assign bmp_show = false
    endif
  endunless

  if bmp_show
    if use_currency
      assign bmp_min_money = product_resource.price_min | money_with_currency
    else
      assign bmp_min_money = product_resource.price_min | money
    endif

    # Placeholder-then-replace mirrors stock Horizon's own handling of this
    # key at blocks/_featured-product-price.liquid:12-13, which keeps the
    # money string out of the t filter's interpolation escaping.
    assign bmp_from = 'content.price_from' | t: price: '__PRICE__'
    echo bmp_from | replace: '__PRICE__', bmp_min_money
  endif
-%}
